---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'; import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro'; import { site, toAbsoluteUrl } from '../config/site';
const schema = {'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'SoftwareApplication','@id':`${site.origin}/#software`,name:site.name,url:`${site.origin}/`,applicationCategory:'UtilitiesApplication',operatingSystem:['Windows 11','Linux'],downloadUrl:site.latestRelease,installUrl:toAbsoluteUrl('/getting-started/')};
---
<BaseLayout title="Download FM AI Assistent for Windows or Linux" description="Get FM AI Assistent from the official GitHub Releases page. Choose a desktop application, native image or Java 25+ JAR." path="/download/" structuredData={schema}>
  <div class="page-shell"><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'Download'}]} /><header class="page-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Official distribution</p><h1>Download FM AI Assistent.</h1><p class="lead">Use the project owner’s GitHub Releases page for the latest published, legitimate builds. The app currently documents Windows 11 and Linux support.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="button" href={site.latestRelease} rel="noopener noreferrer">Open latest release</a><a class="button button-ghost" href={site.releases} rel="noopener noreferrer">View all releases</a></div></header>
    <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><div><h2>Choose the package that fits.</h2></div><p>Exact filenames can change between releases. Read the notes and asset names on GitHub before downloading.</p></div><div class="feature-grid"><article class="info-card"><p class="eyebrow">Recommended</p><h3>Desktop application</h3><p>Best for most users. It packages the runtime and normally opens the local interface automatically.</p><strong>No separate Java install documented.</strong></article><article class="info-card"><p class="eyebrow">Standalone</p><h3>Native image</h3><p>A smaller native executable for the operating system listed in the release asset.</p><strong>No separate Java install documented.</strong></article><article class="info-card"><p class="eyebrow">Portable Java</p><h3>Executable JAR</h3><p>For users who already maintain a Java environment and prefer the JAR distribution.</p><strong>Requires Java 25 or newer.</strong></article></div></section>
    <section class="section content-grid"><div class="prose"><h2>Before you start</h2><ol><li>Download only from the repository linked on this page.</li><li>Extract the desktop package when the release notes require it.</li><li>On Linux, make the downloaded launcher executable if necessary.</li><li>Start FM26, load your save, then launch FM AI Assistent as the same user.</li></ol><pre class="code-block"><code>chmod +x "FM AI Assistent"
# or for the native image
chmod +x fm-ai-assistent
./fm-ai-assistent</code></pre><h2>Using the JAR</h2><pre class="code-block"><code>java -jar fm-ai-assistent.jar</code></pre><p>The interface normally uses <code>http://127.0.0.1:8080</code>. If that port is busy, the app chooses the next available port and records it in the startup log.</p></div><aside class="info-card"><h3>Continue with the guide</h3><p>The getting-started page covers the first data load, provider setup and common failures.</p><a class="text-link" href="/getting-started/">Read getting started →</a><hr style="border-color:var(--line);margin:1.5rem 0"/><h3>Inspect the project</h3><p>The repository is public, but no license file is currently present. Do not assume rights beyond those expressly granted.</p><a class="text-link" href={site.repository} rel="noopener noreferrer">View source on GitHub →</a></aside></section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
